# Jaguar XJ (X350) four-door saloon, 2003-2009.
#
# The aluminium XJ: a retro three-box body with an upright grille and four
# round headlamps in pairs, but a modern aluminium monocoque. The standard
# wheelbase is modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_XJ_(X350)
#
# Dimensions 5.090 x 1.859 x 1.448 m, wheelbase 3.033 m (standard wheelbase;
# the long-wheelbase car is 5.215 m on 3.160 m).
#
# Shape reference: no true level side elevation exists in the pack. The side
# image is a front three-quarter about 35 degrees off the centre line; the
# flank is reconciled against the front and rear three-quarters within the
# published dimensions. The detail image is a full front three-quarter rather
# than a lamp close-up. Both limitations are recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the 2008 model year XJ Collection brochure. Ebony,
# Liquid Silver, Lunar Grey and Botanical Green are brochure names. Weights
# 12, 12, 11, 10, total 45, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 250 km/h. Comfort 140/540, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 140. Classes 3,4.
# Dates 2003-2009 production, road tail staggered 2024-2026.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-xj-x350.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaguar-xj-x350.dae. References:
# citycars/references/jaguar-xj-x350/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: no true side elevation exists; the side image is a front
# three-quarter about 35 degrees off and the detail image is a full front
# three-quarter rather than a lamp close-up. The flank was reconciled against
# both three-quarters and the published dimensions. Lamp, grille and chrome
# detail is simplified at sprite scale.


